For our client located in WESTENDE, we are looking for a CONSTRUCTION MACHINERY MECHANIC.

Our client is a well-established contractor carrying out projects for both the public and private sectors.

As a CONSTRUCTION MACHINERY MECHANIC in WESTENDE, your responsibilities will include:

• Performing inspections and preventive maintenance on construction machinery and trucks;
• Repairing defects and carrying out corrective maintenance on construction machinery and trucks;
• Working both in the workshop and on-site;
• Troubleshooting and resolving electrical, hydraulic and mechanical issues;
• Contributing ideas and suggestions to improve the efficiency and performance of the machinery fleet


As a CONSTRUCTION MACHINERY MECHANIC in WESTENDE, you can identify yourself with the following requirements:

• You have experience as a maintenance technician working on construction machinery and/or trucks;
• You have a good command of Dutch or English;
• You have a valid category B driving licence;
• You have a strong interest in and passion for technology and mechanics, with knowledge of hydraulic and pneumatic systems.

For our client located in WESTENDE we are looking for a ROADWORKER!

Our client is a well-known contractor who does assignments for the government and private sector.

Do you like to roll up your sleeves and work outdoors? Then you are the person we are looking for!

As a ROAD WORKER in WESTENDE this is your job:

• You are responsible for sewerage works;
• You are responsible for placing embroidery;
• Construction of cycle paths, roads and car parks;
• Placing environmental pavements;
• Placing roundabouts and refuges;
• Placing vowels and paving stones;


As a ROAD WORKER in WESTENDE you can find yourself in the following

• You speak Englisch or Dutch;
• You are handy and like to work outside;
• No study requirements - motivation is what we need!

For a well-established company in OOSTENDE, we are looking for an EXPERIENCED WELDER.

Are you an experienced welder who enjoys working independently and taking on technically challenging projects? Do you have experience with semi-automatic welding and are you able to read technical drawings?

Your responsibilities as an EXPERIENCED WELDER in OOSTENDE:

• You carry out semi-automatic welding work;
• You weld metal parts and structures according to technical drawings;
• You are responsible for various repair works. THIS IS NOT A REPETITIVE JOB – you will work on a wide variety of different pieces;
• You work on different projects, ensuring plenty of variety in your daily tasks;
• You ensure a precise finish and maintain high-quality standards;
• You enjoy hands-on work and are not afraid of physically demanding tasks.
As an EXPERIENCED WELDER in OSTEND, you can identify with the following:

• You have extensive and proven experience as a semi-automatic welder;
• You can work independently and accurately;
• You are able to read and interpret technical drawings;
• You are physically fit and enjoy varied work;
• You speak Dutch OR have a very good command of English.

As a Key Account Manager, you will manage a portfolio of approximately 15 to 20 clients, primarily airlines and aircraft maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO) organisations.

Your role combines strategic account management, business development, B2B negotiation and regular international client visits.

Your main responsibilities will include:

•   
Managing, retaining and developing your existing client portfolio;

•   
Overseeing key accounts and strategic client relationships;

•   
Understanding clients' commercial, technical and operational challenges and proposing suitable solutions;

•   
Preparing commercial proposals, responding to tenders and negotiating contracts;

•   
Maintaining regular face-to-face contact with clients and prospects;

•   
Developing new business opportunities;

•   
Preparing sales forecasts and budgets for each client;

•   
Monitoring profitability, volumes and sales performance;

•   
Conducting market analysis and keeping up with developments in the aerospace sector;

•   
Representing the company at industry events and client meetings.

The role involves regular travel across the EMEA region, accounting for approximately 50% of working time, generally on short trips.

This opportunity may particularly appeal to Account Managers, Key Account Managers, Sales Account Managers or Business Development Managers with proven experience in managing strategic client relationships.


•   
You ideally hold a Master's degree in Business, Management or a related field.

•   
You have at least four years of B2B sales experience in an international industrial environment. Experience in the aerospace sector is an advantage.

•   
You have an excellent command of French and English, with C1-level English required. Knowledge of another language used in the EMEA region is an advantage, particularly Arabic.

You stand out through:

•   
A strong customer focus;

•   
Solid negotiation skills;

•   
Excellent interpersonal and presentation skills;

•   
A sound understanding of financial and commercial considerations;

•   
The ability to work in international and multicultural environments;

•   
Autonomy, analytical thinking and effective prioritisation;

•   
The ability to collaborate effectively with a range of internal teams.

WHAT WE OFFER
